.TH TERMTV 1 "2026-08-07" "termtv" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
termtv \- hardware-aware terminal video renderer
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B termtv
[\fICOMMAND\fR] [\fIOPTIONS\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
termtv renders video in a terminal using ANSI half-block characters.
It supports a native \fB.ttv1\fR format and can stream source video or
camera capture through FFmpeg.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B convert \fIinput\fR \fIoutput.ttv\fR
Convert any FFmpeg-readable input to the native \fB.ttv1\fR format.
.TP
.B play \fIfile.ttv\fR
Play a native \fB.ttv1\fR file.
.TP
.B play-source \fIinput\fR
Stream any FFmpeg-readable source directly to the terminal.
.TP
.B playlist list|play \fIfile.m3u\fR
List or play entries from an M3U playlist.
.TP
.B camera on|off|list
Stream, stop, or list V4L2 camera devices.
.TP
.B accel-info
List available hardware acceleration backends.
.TP
.B help
Show usage information.
.TP
.B completions \fIbash|zsh|fish\fR
Print a shell completion script for the requested shell.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-\-width " " \fIN\fR
Output width in terminal cells.
.TP
.BR \-\-height " " \fIN\fR
Output height in terminal cells.
.TP
.BR \-\-fps " " \fIN\fR
Target frames per second.
.TP
.BR \-\-hwaccel " " \fIID\fR
Hardware backend: auto, vaapi, qsv, cuda, vdpau, drm, opencl, vulkan.
.TP
.BR \-\-ambience " " \fIID\fR
Ambience mode: off, pulse, strobe.
.TP
.BR \-\-color
Force ANSI color output.
.TP
.BR \-\-no-color
Disable ANSI color output.
.TP
.BR \-\-device " " \fIPATH\fR
V4L2 device path (camera only).
.TP
.BR \-\-capture-width " " \fIN\fR
Camera capture width.
.TP
.BR \-\-capture-height " " \fIN\fR
Camera capture height.
.TP
.BR \-\-behavior " " \fIlive|photo\fR
Camera behavior.
.TP
.BR \-\-backend " " \fIID\fR
Render backend: \fBansi\fR, \fBkitty\fR, or \fBsixel\fR (default: \fBansi\fR).
Used by \fBplay\fR, \fBplay-source\fR, \fBcamera on\fR, and \fBplaylist play\fR.
.TP
.BR \-\-loop
Restart playback from the first frame when the source ends
(\fBplay\fR, \fBplay-source\fR). Not propagated to individual entries by
\fBplaylist play\fR.
.TP
.BR \-\-volume " " \fIN\fR
Audio volume 0\(en100 (default: 100). Used by \fBplay\fR and \fBplay-source\fR.
.TP
.BR \-\-frames " " \fIN\fR
Render at most \fIN\fR frames and exit (demo mode; default: unlimited).
.TP
.BR \-\-obs
Select the OBS Virtual Camera for \fBcamera on\fR; must be combined with
.BR \-\-device " /dev/videoN" .
.SH KEYBOARD CONTROLS
.TP
.B p\fR, \fBspace
Pause/resume playback.
.TP
.BR [\fR, \fB]
Seek \(mi10s / +10s.
.TP
.B a
Toggle ambience mode (\fBplay-source\fR only).
.TP
.B q
Quit playback.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ./.termtv.toml
Local configuration file.
.TP
.I ~/.config/termtv/config.toml
User configuration file.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success.
.TP
.B 1
An error occurred: unknown command, missing or invalid argument, unreadable
input, or playback/convert failure. The specific failure is reported on
stderr as a \fBtermtv_event=\fR diagnostic.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
# Convert a video to the native format, then play it
termtv convert clip.mp4 clip.ttv
termtv play clip.ttv

# Stream a source directly, looping with the kitty backend
termtv play-source clip.mp4 \-\-loop \-\-backend kitty

# Stream with quiet audio at half volume
termtv play-source clip.mp4 \-\-volume 50

# Convert for a small terminal with a fixed frame rate
termtv convert clip.mp4 clip.ttv \-\-width 80 \-\-height 24 \-\-fps 30

# List a playlist, then play it
termtv playlist list mix.m3u
termtv playlist play mix.m3u

# Stream the OBS Virtual Camera
termtv camera on \-\-obs \-\-device /dev/video2

# Check which hardware accelerators are usable
termtv accel\-info

# Render the built-in demo for 100 frames
termtv \-\-frames 100
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR ffmpeg (1)
